<h1>About Gift of the Givers</h1>

<h2>Serving Humanity. Restoring Dignity.</h2>

<p>
    Gift of the Givers Foundation is a South African humanitarian organisation established in 1992. The organisation responds to emergencies and supports vulnerable communities through humanitarian relief, disaster response and long-term development initiatives.
</p>

<p>
    Its work is guided by the principle <strong>“Best among people are those who benefit mankind.”</strong> Assistance is provided on a humanitarian and unconditional basis, with a focus on protecting dignity and supporting people affected by disasters, poverty and other difficult circumstances.
</p>

<h3>Our Areas of Focus</h3>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Disaster Response</strong> – providing emergency assistance, supplies and support to communities affected by disasters and crises.</li>
    <li><strong>Hunger Alleviation</strong> – supporting food distribution, feeding schemes and agricultural initiatives.</li>
    <li><strong>Water Provision</strong> – helping communities access safe and reliable water through water delivery, boreholes and water infrastructure.</li>
    <li><strong>Healthcare</strong> – supporting healthcare services, medical interventions, equipment and vulnerable patients.</li>
    <li><strong>Education</strong> – supporting learners through educational resources, bursaries and improvements to school infrastructure.</li>
    <li><strong>Human Development</strong> – supporting initiatives that improve living conditions, develop skills and empower vulnerable communities.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Our Mission</h3>

<p>
    To respond quickly and effectively to humanitarian needs while helping vulnerable communities recover, rebuild and develop sustainable solutions for the future.
</p>

<h3>Our Relief Management System</h3>

<p>
    This application provides a prototype digital platform for coordinating disaster-relief activities. It brings together information about relief projects, donations, volunteers, resources and beneficiaries in one central system.
</p>

<p>
    The goal is to improve visibility of relief operations, support better coordination and provide a foundation for more efficient disaster-response management.
</p>
